The objective was not simply to switch a fan ON and OFF.

I wanted to explore how an embedded controller could retrofit an existing
household appliance without replacing its original control mechanism.
I want to improve better comfort with fan speed control  without manual adjustment at night with low cost

Instead of electronically redesigning the entire fan, the system uses a
servo motor as an actuator to physically operate the existing regulator.

This approach combines:

Sensor → Embedded Controller → Control Algorithm → Actuator → Appliance
